<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beauvais</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Caesaromagus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beauvais is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oise">Oise</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> in Hauts-de-France. It grew from Caesaromagus, the Roman chief town of the Bellovaci, and became a bishopric. Its Gothic cathedral of Saint-Pierre has the highest choir vault in the world, which partly collapsed in 1284, and its tapestry manufactory was founded in 1664.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beauvais.jpg" alt="Beauvais" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diliff · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beauvais_Cathedral_Exterior_1,_Picardy,_France_-_Diliff.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
